SUMMARY:Nature Play Day at the Art Museum
DESCRIPTION:*This program is taking place at the North Carolina Museum of Art. We will be set up near the Welcome Center.*  \nCome out and play! We will be stocking part of the Art Museum’s outdoor park with extra special materials and supplies to encourage nature exploration and outdoor play! A Prairie Ridge play facilitator will be present to help you play your way. Supplies may vary each month\, but may include fun things like fort-building equipment\, puppets and costumes\, bubbles\, paint\, and more.  \nThis is a free\, drop-in event. Staff and supplies will be available from 10:00am -12:00pm. This program is completely outdoors\, so come dressed for the weather and ready to potentially get messy! Everyone is welcome at this program\, but it has been designed especially for kids 7 and younger.  \nThe North Carolina Museum of Art is located at 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, NC 27607. Please contact kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org with any questions! 
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/nature-play-day-at-the-art-museum/
LOCATION:North Carolina Museum of Art\, 2110 Blue Ridge Rd\, Raleigh\, 27607
CATEGORIES:Children,Nature Play Days,Outdoor Experiences,Walk-up Programs
ORGANIZER;CN="Kiersten%20Bowser":MAILTO:kiersten.bowser@naturalsciences.org
END:VEVENT
